(# Forward difference under a local derivative variation bound) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Define the forward-difference approximation for a real function f at x) Tj T*
(with step h as \(f\(x+h\) - f\(x\)\) / h.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Prove that for every f and D from real numbers to real numbers and every) Tj T*
(real x, h, L, the following assumptions imply the stated error bound:) Tj T*
(- h > 0 and L >= 0;) Tj T*
(- f is continuous on the closed interval [x, x+h];) Tj T*
(- f has derivative D\(t\) at every t in the open interval \(x, x+h\);) Tj T*
(- for every t in the open interval \(x, x+h\),) Tj T*
(  |D\(t\) - D\(x\)| <= L * |t-x|.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The absolute difference between the defined forward difference and D\(x\)) Tj T*
(is at most L*h. Here D\(x\) is the reference value in the variation bound.) Tj T*
(No derivative at either endpoint is required by this task.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
